  "body": "## What happens\n\nEach 2D and 3D milling path starts with a rapid from (WCS X0 Y0, clearance) to the entry point of the operation. The machine never makes this move: after a tool change the X/Y position of the tool is not known.\n\n- The viewport draws a rapid line from the WCS origin.\n- The simulation moves the tool from the WCS origin. Between two operations it goes from the end of the first operation to the WCS origin, then to the entry of the next one.\n- The fixture checks and the link router judge this move. If the line from the WCS origin to the entry strikes a fixture, `plan_links` lifts the link at the WCS origin. The post then writes `G00 Z<H>` and `G00 X0. Y0. Z<H>`: a real first move to the WCS origin. A fixture at the WCS corner can also give a false refusal or a false fixture hit.\n\n## Where\n\n- `crates/app/src/operation/generate.rs:3109-3117`: `path.seat_approach(Point3::new(0.0, 0.0, hl.clearance), [o.x, o.y])` puts the start at the WCS origin (#2382).\n- `crates/cl/src/cl/path_approach.rs:30-49`: `Toolpath::seat_approach`.\n- `crates/app/src/operation/fixture_route.rs:186-229`: `plan` lifts the link at the start X/Y.\n- The seeds: `PathBuilder::approached(Point3::new(0.0, 0.0, p.clearance_z))` in `crates/motion/src/machining2d/*.rs` and `crates/motion/src/finishing3d/*.rs`.\n- The tests that lock the current behaviour: `crates/app/tests/wcs_start.rs:143-170` (`opens_at`) and `crates/cl/tests/origin_approach.rs:62-99`.\n\n## What is expected\n\n- The WCS is only the reference of the coordinates. No move of the path starts or ends at the WCS origin unless the operation cuts there.\n- The opening rapid starts over its own entry point, on the clearance plane: `from.x == to.x` and `from.y == to.y`. It stays a rapid (the approach law of #690 and #697).\n- The posted program does not change when no fixture is struck. The current goldens stay byte-identical.\n- With a fixture, the link router does not lift a link at the WCS origin. No `X0 Y0` block is posted for it.\n- The 3+2 frame case and the yaw case keep their local frame (the call site reads the frame before the seat).\n\n## Done when\n\n- `seat_approach` seats the start over the end X/Y of the opening rapid, not over the WCS origin. Alternative: it is removed and the seeds do the same. Record the choice in `docs/decisions/`.\n- `wcs_start.rs` asserts the new law for a face (2D), a 3D finish and a drill, with the WCS at the stock centre and at the stock corner. The opening rapid has no X/Y length, and no move starts at the WCS origin.\n- A new pinning test in `crates/app/tests/` puts a fixture box between the WCS origin and the entry. The posted program has no `X0 Y0` block and no fixture refusal.\n- `crates/cl/tests/origin_approach.rs` is updated for the new law.\n- The posted goldens in `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/` do not change.\n\nRefs #2899\n",
